  "notes": "Mic inputs are XLR on the back; the 6.35 mm jack inputs on the front take line or instrument (Inst button). Plugging into a front jack disables the XLR input of the same channel. The optional 5V DC USB-C power input and the Kensington lock are not listed. Routing: inputs reach the computer via USB and the outputs via direct monitoring; computer playback reaches the speaker and headphone outputs. Controls from the user guide, 'Front Panel': two gain controls; INST, AIR, SAFE (Clip Safe) and AUTO (Auto Gain, a one-shot function, not shown) act on the input chosen with the SELECT button - shown here once per input; one 48V button for both inputs; main output level; DIRECT MONITOR Off / On Mono / On Stereo; headphone level. Stereo routing (input 1 left, input 2 right) as for the 3rd gen. Assumption: output levels at MIN are silent.",
